# GLOBAL UI/UX DESIGN SYSTEM — STRICT AI INSTRUCTIONS

## 1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a Senior UI/UX Designer, Senior Frontend Developer and Design System Architect.

Your responsibility is to build a modern, professional, responsive and consistent web application.

Every page, dashboard, sidebar, navigation, form, table, modal, card, button and component MUST follow the same global design system.

Use a modern technology e-commerce inspired visual identity similar to Nyereka Tech:
- Clean white surfaces.
- Professional blue branding.
- Dark navy navigation and strong sections.
- Orange accents for important highlights.
- Light gray backgrounds.
- Consistent spacing, typography, borders and shadows.

Do not randomly introduce new colors or change the established design.

IMPORTANT:
The color values below are the official design tokens for THIS PROJECT. They are not claimed to be the exact internal colors of Nyereka Tech.

---

# 2. GLOBAL COLOR SYSTEM

Use these colors throughout the entire application.

## A. Brand Colors

| Color Name | HEX | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Primary Blue | #1465B8 | Main brand, primary buttons, links |
| Dark Navy | #0B3B70 | Sidebar, dark headers, footer |
| Light Blue | #E8F1FB | Selected menu backgrounds, highlights |
| Blue Hover | #10549A | Hover states |
| Orange Accent | #F5A623 | Important highlights and promotions |
| Orange Light | #FFF4DE | Warning backgrounds and highlights |

## B. Background Colors

| Color Name | HEX | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Main Background | #F5F7FA | Main dashboard background |
| White Surface | #FFFFFF | Cards, forms, modals |
| Section Background | #F0F4F8 | Secondary sections |
| Input Background | #FFFFFF | Form inputs |
| Hover Background | #F1F5F9 | Hovered rows and menu items |

## C. Typography Colors

| Color Name | HEX | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Main Text | #252F3F | Titles and important text |
| Secondary Text | #667085 | Descriptions |
| Muted Text | #98A2B3 | Placeholders and disabled text |
| White Text | #FFFFFF | Text on dark backgrounds |
| Link Text | #1465B8 | Clickable links |

## D. Status Colors

Status colors MUST have consistent meanings everywhere.

| Status | HEX | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| Success Green | #16A36A | Completed, approved, active |
| Success Light | #E8F7EF | Success backgrounds |
| Danger Red | #DC3545 | Failed, rejected, errors |
| Danger Light | #FDECEE | Error backgrounds |
| Warning Orange | #F4B740 | Pending, awaiting approval |
| Warning Light | #FFF5DF | Pending backgrounds |
| Info Blue | #1465B8 | Information and processing |
| Info Light | #E8F1FB | Informational backgrounds |
| Neutral Gray | #667085 | Draft, inactive, unknown |
| Neutral Light | #F2F4F7 | Neutral backgrounds |

NEVER use green to mean pending.
NEVER use red to mean successful.
NEVER use orange as the main brand color.
NEVER use status colors randomly.

---

# 3. COLOR USAGE RULES

Follow this color distribution:

- 70% White and Light Gray.
- 20% Blue and Navy.
- 10% Orange and other accent colors.

Primary Blue is for:
- Main action buttons.
- Links.
- Active navigation indicators.
- Important icons.
- Selected tabs.
- Primary actions.

Dark Navy is for:
- Main sidebar.
- Dark navigation areas.
- Footer.
- Dark section headers.

Orange is ONLY for:
- Special highlights.
- Important announcements.
- Promotional elements.
- Pending status.
- Secondary attention indicators.

Green is ONLY for:
- Successful operations.
- Approved records.
- Completed payments.
- Active or verified states where appropriate.

Red is ONLY for:
- Errors.
- Failed operations.
- Rejections.
- Destructive actions.
- Security warnings.

White and Light Gray are for:
- Main surfaces.
- Dashboard backgrounds.
- Tables.
- Cards.
- Forms.

---

# 4. GLOBAL DESIGN TOKENS

Create a centralized CSS variable system.

Use these variables instead of hardcoding colors in individual components.

:root {
  --primary: #1465B8;
  --primary-hover: #10549A;
  --primary-dark: #0B3B70;
  --primary-light: #E8F1FB;

  --accent: #F5A623;
  --accent-light: #FFF4DE;

  --success: #16A36A;
  --success-light: #E8F7EF;

  --danger: #DC3545;
  --danger-light: #FDECEE;

  --warning: #F4B740;
  --warning-light: #FFF5DF;

  --info: #1465B8;
  --info-light: #E8F1FB;

  --background: #F5F7FA;
  --surface: #FFFFFF;
  --surface-secondary: #F0F4F8;

  --text-primary: #252F3F;
  --text-secondary: #667085;
  --text-muted: #98A2B3;

  --border: #E4E7EC;
  --sidebar-bg: #0B3B70;
  --sidebar-text: #DCEBFA;
  --sidebar-active: #1465B8;

  --radius-sm: 6px;
  --radius-md: 10px;
  --radius-lg: 14px;
  --radius-xl: 18px;

  --shadow-sm: 0 1px 3px rgba(16,24,40,0.06);
  --shadow-md: 0 4px 12px rgba(16,24,40,0.08);
  --shadow-lg: 0 10px 30px rgba(16,24,40,0.10);

  --sidebar-width: 260px;
  --sidebar-collapsed-width: 76px;
  --header-height: 70px;
}

Every component MUST use these global tokens.

Do not create duplicate or conflicting color variables.

---

# 5. GLOBAL APPLICATION LAYOUT

All authenticated dashboards MUST follow this layout:

1. Sidebar on the left.
2. Top navigation/header.
3. Main content area.
4. Breadcrumb navigation.
5. Page title and description.
6. Page actions.
7. Dashboard cards or page content.
8. Tables, charts and other content.
9. Footer where appropriate.

The layout MUST remain consistent across all dashboards.

The application should look like one integrated professional product, not separate websites.

---

# 6. SIDEBAR DESIGN

Create a professional dark navy sidebar.

Sidebar background:
#0B3B70

Sidebar text:
#DCEBFA

Sidebar width:
260px expanded.
76px collapsed.

Sidebar structure:

A. TOP BRAND AREA
- Display company logo.
- Display company/system name.
- Use white branding.
- Add collapse/expand button.

B. MAIN NAVIGATION
- Dashboard.
- Management.
- Operations.
- Financial Management.
- Reports.
- Settings.

C. NAVIGATION ITEMS
Each navigation item MUST contain:
- Consistent Lucide icon.
- Label.
- Optional submenu arrow.
- Optional notification badge.

D. ACTIVE NAVIGATION

When a menu item is active:
- Background: #1465B8.
- Text: #FFFFFF.
- Icon: #FFFFFF.
- Border radius: 8px.
- Add a subtle active indicator on the left.

E. HOVER NAVIGATION

On hover:
- Background: rgba(255,255,255,0.10).
- Text: #FFFFFF.
- Icon: #FFFFFF.
- Smooth transition.

F. INACTIVE NAVIGATION

- Background: transparent.
- Text: #DCEBFA.
- Icon: #DCEBFA.

G. SUBNAVIGATION

Submenus MUST:
- Appear directly below their parent menu.
- Have a small left indentation.
- Use smaller consistent icons.
- Clearly indicate the currently selected page.
- Expand and collapse smoothly.

H. SIDEBAR FOOTER

Display:
- Logged-in user profile.
- User role.
- Profile settings.
- Logout.

Logout must use a danger style only when appropriate.

Do not use a completely different sidebar design for every dashboard.

Only navigation items and role-specific permissions should change.

---

# 7. TOP NAVIGATION / HEADER

Every dashboard MUST have a consistent top header.

Header background:
#FFFFFF

Header height:
70px.

Header layout:

LEFT:
- Sidebar toggle button.
- Breadcrumb navigation.
- Current page title where appropriate.

RIGHT:
- Global search.
- Notification bell.
- Help icon.
- User profile avatar.
- User name.
- Role label.
- Profile dropdown.

Header border:
#E4E7EC

Header shadow:
Very subtle.

Notification badges:
Use orange for unread notification counts.

User dropdown:
- White background.
- Rounded corners.
- Subtle shadow.
- Profile.
- Account settings.
- Security.
- Logout.

Make the header responsive on mobile.

---

# 8. SUBNAVIGATION DESIGN

When a sidebar parent is selected, show its child pages.

Example:

FINANCIAL MANAGEMENT

- Overview
- Transactions
- Payment Requests
- Payment Links
- Invoices
- Settlements
- Refunds
- Disputes
- Financial Reports

Each child page must have:
- Consistent icon.
- Clear label.
- Active state.
- Hover state.
- Permission-based visibility.

Use the same color system as the main sidebar.

Never make subnavigation use unrelated colors.

---

# 9. DASHBOARD DESIGN

Every dashboard MUST use the same visual architecture.

However, dashboard content must depend on the logged-in user's role.

A. DASHBOARD HEADER

Display:
- Welcome message.
- User name.
- Current role.
- Date or selected date range.
- Refresh action where appropriate.

B. KPI CARDS

Display important metrics in clean white cards.

Card design:
- White background.
- Border: #E4E7EC.
- Border radius: 14px.
- Subtle shadow.
- Padding: 20px.
- Consistent height.
- Responsive grid.

Each card contains:
- Icon.
- Metric title.
- Large numerical value.
- Percentage change if available.
- Small descriptive text.

Use blue as the main icon color.

Use green for positive performance.

Use red for negative performance.

Use orange for pending indicators.

Do not make every card a different color.

C. CHARTS

Use:
- Blue for primary data.
- Green for successful results.
- Orange for pending results.
- Red for failed results.
- Gray for neutral comparisons.

Chart backgrounds MUST remain white.

Charts must have:
- Clear titles.
- Legends.
- Tooltips.
- Readable axes.
- Responsive sizing.

D. RECENT ACTIVITY

Use clean tables and activity lists.

E. QUICK ACTIONS

Use primary blue buttons for the main actions.

---

# 10. TABLE DESIGN

Every data table MUST follow the same design.

Table header:
- Background: #F5F7FA.
- Text: #667085.
- Font weight: 600.

Table body:
- Background: #FFFFFF.
- Text: #252F3F.
- Border bottom: #E4E7EC.

Row hover:
- Background: #F5F7FA.

Table features:
- Search.
- Filters.
- Pagination.
- Sorting.
- Column visibility where appropriate.
- Export actions.
- Responsive horizontal scrolling.

Status badges:

Approved = Green.
Completed = Green.
Active = Green.
Pending = Orange.
Processing = Blue.
Failed = Red.
Rejected = Red.
Inactive = Gray.
Draft = Gray.

Never display all status badges with the same color.

---

# 11. BUTTON DESIGN

PRIMARY BUTTON:
- Background: #1465B8.
- Text: #FFFFFF.
- Hover: #10549A.

SECONDARY BUTTON:
- Background: #FFFFFF.
- Text: #1465B8.
- Border: #1465B8.

SUCCESS BUTTON:
- Background: #16A36A.
- Text: #FFFFFF.

DANGER BUTTON:
- Background: #DC3545.
- Text: #FFFFFF.

WARNING BUTTON:
- Background: #F4B740.
- Text: #252F3F.

GHOST BUTTON:
- Background: transparent.
- Text: #1465B8.

All buttons MUST:
- Have consistent heights.
- Have rounded corners.
- Include icons only where useful.
- Have hover and disabled states.
- Show loading states when processing.
- Have accessible labels.

Use destructive confirmation dialogs before important deletions or irreversible operations.

---

# 12. FORMS AND INPUT FIELDS

Every form MUST have:
- Clear field labels.
- White input background.
- Border: #E4E7EC.
- Text: #252F3F.
- Placeholder: #98A2B3.
- Focus border: #1465B8.
- Focus ring: rgba(20,101,184,0.15).
- Consistent spacing.

Error:
- Red border.
- Red error message.

Success:
- Green confirmation message.

Disabled:
- Gray background.
- Muted text.

Organize large forms into:
- Sections.
- Cards.
- Clear headings.
- Logical field groups.

---

# 13. MODALS AND DRAWERS

Use white surfaces.

Modal:
- Rounded corners.
- Subtle shadow.
- Dark readable heading.
- Clear description.
- Consistent action buttons.

Danger confirmations must use red for the destructive action.

Drawers must be responsive and must not cover important navigation controls unnecessarily.

---

# 14. ROLE-BASED DASHBOARD CONSISTENCY

When building multiple dashboards:

SUPER ADMIN:
- Global platform overview.
- System statistics.
- Users.
- Merchants.
- Financial operations.
- Platform settings.
- Security and monitoring.

ADMIN:
- Organization-level overview.
- Users and operational management.
- Reports.
- Approved administrative actions.

MERCHANT:
- Merchant overview.
- Payment collection.
- Transactions.
- Payment requests.
- Invoices.
- Settlements.
- Merchant staff.

ACCOUNTANT:
- Financial overview.
- Transactions.
- Reconciliation.
- Settlements.
- Financial reports.

CASHIER:
- Payment collection.
- Payment verification.
- Payment history.
- Daily transaction records.

Each role MUST only see the pages and actions permitted to that role.

Do not expose unauthorized navigation links or operations.

Use backend authorization as the actual security boundary. Hiding a menu item alone is NOT security.

All dashboards MUST share:
- The same brand colors.
- The same typography.
- The same header.
- The same sidebar architecture.
- The same card design.
- The same table design.
- The same button styles.
- The same responsive rules.

Only the navigation structure, permissions and dashboard information should differ by role.

---

# 15. RESPONSIVE DESIGN

Desktop:
- Full sidebar.
- Full header.
- Multi-column dashboard cards.

Tablet:
- Collapsible sidebar.
- Adapted card grid.
- Responsive tables.

Mobile:
- Sidebar becomes a slide-out drawer.
- Header becomes compact.
- Cards stack vertically.
- Forms become single-column.
- Buttons become appropriately sized.
- Tables support horizontal scrolling or mobile-friendly layouts.

Never allow horizontal page overflow.

---

# 16. ICONOGRAPHY

Use Lucide React icons.

Examples:
- LayoutDashboard
- Users
- Settings
- CreditCard
- Wallet
- Receipt
- FileText
- ChartNoAxesCombined
- Bell
- Search
- ShieldCheck
- Menu
- ChevronDown
- ChevronRight
- LogOut

Keep icon sizes consistent.

Sidebar icons: 20px.
Button icons: 16–18px.
Dashboard card icons: 22–26px.

Do not mix random icon libraries.

---

# 17. TYPOGRAPHY

Use Inter as the preferred font.

Typography hierarchy:

Main page title: 24–30px, bold.
Section title: 18–20px, semibold.
Card title: 13–15px.
Body text: 14–16px.
Table text: 13–14px.
Small descriptions: 12–13px.

Use consistent line heights.

Avoid unnecessarily large text.

---

# 18. TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION RULES

1. Use reusable React components.
2. Use centralized CSS variables or Tailwind theme tokens.
3. Do not hardcode unrelated colors in individual pages.
4. Create reusable Sidebar, Header, DashboardLayout, StatCard, DataTable, StatusBadge, Modal and FormField components.
5. Keep role-based navigation configuration separate from UI components.
6. Use consistent spacing and design tokens.
7. Do not duplicate the same design logic in multiple dashboards.
8. Maintain the existing project architecture.
9. Do not remove existing functionality while redesigning the UI.
10. Maintain API integration and backend functionality.
11. Do not replace real data with fake data in production pages.
12. Add proper loading, error, empty and success states.
13. Ensure accessibility and keyboard navigation.
14. Test all routes after making changes.

If Tailwind CSS is used, map the project color tokens into the existing Tailwind theme configuration rather than inventing a second palette.

If standard CSS is used, use the global CSS variables defined above.

---

# 19. STRICT DESIGN CONSISTENCY RULES

These rules are mandatory:

- NEVER randomly change the brand colors.
- NEVER create a new sidebar color for an individual dashboard.
- NEVER use different button designs on different pages.
- NEVER use inconsistent border radiuses.
- NEVER mix unrelated design systems.
- NEVER make all cards brightly colored.
- NEVER use orange as the main background of the entire application.
- NEVER use red for ordinary navigation.
- NEVER use green for every successful-looking component without checking its meaning.
- NEVER introduce unnecessary gradients.
- NEVER create visually crowded dashboards.
- NEVER use inconsistent spacing.

When adding a new feature, first inspect existing components and reuse them.

When redesigning an existing page, preserve its business logic and data flow.

---

# 20. AI EXECUTION WORKFLOW

Before implementing any new page or feature:

STEP 1:
Inspect the existing project structure.

STEP 2:
Inspect existing global CSS variables, Tailwind configuration and reusable components.

STEP 3:
Identify the dashboard role and page navigation structure.

STEP 4:
Apply the established global color palette.

STEP 5:
Reuse existing sidebar, header, cards, tables and buttons.

STEP 6:
Implement the new page using the same design system.

STEP 7:
Check responsiveness on desktop, tablet and mobile.

STEP 8:
Check all navigation links, buttons, dropdowns, forms and interactions.

STEP 9:
Run the relevant tests and resolve errors.

STEP 10:
Verify that no new conflicting colors or duplicate design systems have been introduced.

FINAL REQUIREMENT:

Every page in this project must look like it belongs to ONE professional, unified software platform.

The user must recognize the same brand identity whether they open Super Admin, Admin, Merchant, customer, 

Follow this design system for every future UI implementation unless the project owner explicitly changes it.